1
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:25,130
<i>They are an army unlike any other...</i>

2
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:29,000
<i>crusading across the stars 
toward a place called UnderVerse,</i>

3
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:31,010
<i>their promised land...</i>

4
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:34,380
<i>a constellation of dark new worlds.</i>

5
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:36,890
<i>Necromongers, they're called.</i>

6
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:41,350
<i>And if they cannot convert you, 
they will kill you.</i>

7
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:45,980
<i>Leading them, the Lord Marshal.</i>

8
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:50,150
<i>He alone has made a pilgrimage 
to the gates of the UnderVerse...</i>

9
00:01:50,190 --> 00:01:53,450
<i>and returned a different being.</i>

10
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:56,780
<i>Stronger. Stranger.</i>

11
00:01:56,870 --> 00:02:00,160
<i>Half alive and half...</i>

12
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,960
<i>something else.</i>

13
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:50,750
Linin' him up for you. Port-side 
shot comin' up. Steady. Here we go.

14
00:02:57,970 --> 00:03:00,760
Steady.

15
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:03,890
<i>Take it. Take it!</i>

16
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:06,390
Take the shot!

17
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,110
Shit! 
Toombs, we're runnin' out of road!

18
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:13,400
Shut up! I got it! Again!

19
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:18,740
Now!

20
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,910
Toombs!

21
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:38,590
Riddick.

22
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:54,730
<i>Three meters clearance port-side. 
One and a half meters starboard.</i>

23
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:57,280
We got a choke point comin' up.

24
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:12,330
<i>What the shit was that?</i>

25
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:17,300
Tags, you got eyes on Riddick?

26
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:20,180
Tags?

27
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:26,260
Jesus.

28
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:29,270
He just ghosted two guys, 
and I never even saw him.

29
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:33,230
What do you think, Toombs? 
I mean, maybe we oughta just...

30
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,730
I think you're my new gunner.

31
00:04:35,110 --> 00:04:36,940
Grab a Gat.

32
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:46,490
Stay on top of him this time.

33
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:18,070
<i>You made three mistakes.</i>

34
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:23,110
First, you took the job.

35
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,200
Second, you came light.

36
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:29,870
<i>A four-man crew for me? 
Fuckin' insulting.</i>

37
00:05:29,950 --> 00:05:33,080
<i>But the worst mistake you made...</i>

38
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,130
<i>Empty gun rack.</i>

39
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,890
- What's the bounty on my head? 
- One mil.

40
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:52,230
- One-point-five. 
- What slam pays 1.5 for a convict?

41
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,560
Private party.

42
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,610
Hey, hey, hey, hey! 
Guy, guy! Easy! Anonymous.

43
00:05:57,650 --> 00:06:01,030
- That's what the sheet said. 
- What planet?

44
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,360
Helion Prime.

45
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:14,580
Whoa. Where you going'? 
Last question.

46
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:18,290
And you better get this one right, merc.

47
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:20,300
Whose ship is this?

48
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:22,880
Mine?

49
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,510
Wrong Answer

50
00:06:43,530 --> 00:06:46,030
<i>Knew they'd come for me.</i>

51
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:49,070
<i>Took 'em five years, but I knew.</i>

52
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:53,830
<i>You don't expect these mercs 
to have any honor, any code.</i>

53
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:59,960
<i>But this new bounty from a holy man,</i>

54
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:03,000
<i>a guy whose neck I saved...</i>

55
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:06,380
<i>Well, lesson learned.</i>

56
00:07:06,470 --> 00:07:09,180
<i>No such word as "friend. "</i>

57
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:12,510
<i>It can only end bad 
when you let someone get too close.</i>

58
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,890
<i>Bad for them.</i>

59
00:07:15,890 --> 00:07:19,310
<i>So now it's back to civilization</i>

60
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:23,150
<i> all the brightness... 
and everything I hate.</i>

61
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:27,650
Just wanted to be left alone

62
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:31,410
<i>Helion Prime is on alert condition four.</i>

63
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:41,250
<i>Unrecognized craft. You need to follow me 
to Spaceport Six for security inspections.</i>

64
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:44,590
<i>Hey! Do you hear me?</i>

65
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:47,300
<i>Follow me to Spaceport Six now!</i>

66
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:39,680
Imam, pray for us.

67
00:08:39,770 --> 00:08:43,020
<i>It was confirmed 
two seasons back. Yes.</i>

68
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:45,440
<i>They're coming here. 
I mean, are we next?</i>

69
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,480
<i>Militants storm...</i>

70
00:08:47,570 --> 00:08:50,700
<i>Yes. But going to the underground 
shelters if it happens...</i>

71
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,990
<i>You're right. 
That's what I thought too.</i>

72
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:55,530
<i>Are you staying or leaving?</i>

73
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:57,910
<i>It's the end of everything. 
Everything!</i>

74
00:08:57,990 --> 00:09:01,460
<i>Well, my neighbours... 
Half my street is gone.</i>

75
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:03,460
What are we gonna do? 
I don't know. I don't know.

76
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:05,460
<i>Hood of the devil. 
That's what someone called 'em.</i>

77
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:07,630
Them? Who is them? 
Some kind of new creature...

78
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:09,670
This is nonsense. 
It's all nonsense.

79
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:13,680
<i>So tall that it touches the clouds.</i>

80
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:18,100
And there's nothing around this 
statue, this colossus. Nothing left.

81
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,390
It's their calling card.

82
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:34,070
<i>Did you know all your doors were locked?</i>

83
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:41,540
<i>Five years ago,</i>

84
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:44,500
<i>I took two people off that planet...</i>

85
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:48,800
<i>A kid, Jack, 
who everyone else thought was a boy,</i>

86
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,550
<i>and a holy man...</i>

87
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:53,590
<i>searching for New Mecca.</i>

88
00:09:56,430 --> 00:10:01,180
<i>I told one man...</i>

89
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:04,440
where I might go.

90
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:08,440
I showed trust to one man.

91
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,990
Did I make a mistake, Imam?

92
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:14,400
There is no simple answer.

93
00:10:14,490 --> 00:10:19,160
Whatever was said 
was meant to give us a chance...

94
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:21,240
a fighting chance.

95
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:25,120
Were it not for the threat of invasion, 
I never would have betrayed you.

96
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:30,880
So now who do I have to kill 
to get this payday off my head?

97
00:10:46,770 --> 00:10:51,320
<i>It is said the comet 
always precedes them...</i>

98
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,860
these world-enders.

99
00:10:55,950 --> 00:10:57,910
The Coalsack planets are gone.

100
00:10:57,950 --> 00:11:00,780
<i>Eight million settlers missing.</i>

101
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:04,500
<i>The entire Aquilan System is gone too.</i>

102
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:08,960
Helion Prime shares its sunlight 
with all worlds nearby.

103
00:11:11,090 --> 00:11:15,800
If we fall, they fall.

104
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,220
And after that...

105
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:21,430
My God, 
how do I save my family?

106
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:28,600
<i>Have you heard anything I've said?</i>

107
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:34,570
You said it's all circling the 
drain... the whole universe.

108
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,570
<i>- Right? 
- That's right.</i>

109
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,750
Had to end sometime.

110
00:12:05,310 --> 00:12:07,310
The one you want is now here.

111
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:27,700
And whose throat is this?

112
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:33,380
If you cut my throat, I'll not be able to 
rescind the offer that brought you here.

113
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:35,960
Nor tell you why it's so vital 
that you did come.

114
00:12:36,050 --> 00:12:38,970
The blade comes off 
when the bounty comes off.

115
00:12:39,010 --> 00:12:42,640
This is Aereon, 
an envoy from the Elemental race.

116
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:45,100
She means you no harm.

117
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:52,650
There are very few of us who have met 
a Necromonger and lived to speak of it.

118
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,770
Necromonger.

119
00:12:54,860 --> 00:13:00,150
It is the name that will convert 
or kill every last human life...

120
00:13:00,450 --> 00:13:01,400
<i>There is a story, Riddick, 
of young male Furyans...</i>

121
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,070
<i>There is a story, Riddick, 
of young male Furyans...</i>

122
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:05,070
<i>There is a story, Riddick, 
of young male Furyans...</i>

123
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,660
strangled at birth...

124
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,950
strangled with their own cords.

125
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:14,290
When Aereon told this story 
to the Helion leaders,

126
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:16,460
I told her of you.

127
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,630
- What do you know of your early years? 
- Do you remember your home world?

128
00:13:19,710 --> 00:13:22,180
- Where it was? 
- Have you met any others?

129
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:24,260
Others like yourself.

130
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:30,930
Sister, they don't know 
what to do with just one of me.

131
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:33,480
<i>Open up in there!</i>

132
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,190
<i>- Stand back! 
- Open up!</i>

133
00:13:35,190 --> 00:13:39,570
I will send them away. 
But wait one minute, please.

134
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:42,780
<i>Will you wait one minute 
to save worlds?</i>

135
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:47,240
Not my fight.

136
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,580
So, you will leave us 
to our fate,

137
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,960
<i>just like you did her.</i>

138
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:55,250
<i>Break it down!</i>

139
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,090
Get him!

140
00:13:58,170 --> 00:14:00,510
Come. Let us try to send them away.

141
00:14:03,970 --> 00:14:06,220
<i>Move it. Come on. 
Leave us alone!</i>

142
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:11,850
There is no one here!

143
00:14:11,930 --> 00:14:15,730
<i>You don't understand. 
He can help us! He can help us!</i>

144
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:20,900
<i>Go!</i>

145
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:29,240
You're not afraid of the dark, are you?

146
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,180
<i>- Get him! 
- Where is he?</i>

147
00:14:52,270 --> 00:14:54,600
In there!

148
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:24,050
You mentioned her.

149
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:27,010
She, uh...

150
00:15:27,050 --> 00:15:29,010
She went looking for you.

151
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:32,470
People died. 
She went to prison.

152
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:36,350
I... I don't remember where.

153
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:42,820
But it was a world so hot 
you could not survive on the surface.

154
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:46,360
- Crematoria. 
- Young Jack.

155
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,660
She thought of you 
as her older brother.

156
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:51,740
- She worshipped you. 
- You were supposed to watch her.

157
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:55,540
<i>She never forgave you...</i>

158
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:58,080
for leaving just when 
she needed you most.

159
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:02,960
She needed to stay away 
from me.

160
00:16:03,710 --> 00:16:05,840
You all do

161
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:18,020
Furyans. 
Defiant to the end.

162
00:16:54,890 --> 00:16:57,720
No, no.

163
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:00,310
We go to the shelter.

164
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:02,850
We take only ourselves.

165
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Stay close.

166
00:17:58,490 --> 00:18:01,080
<i>No!</i>

167
00:19:12,230 --> 00:19:14,860
<i>Flight leaders, get all squads 
off the ground now.</i>

168
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:17,780
<i>We have heavy inbound.</i>

169
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:20,990
<i>Follow me in!</i>

170
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:41,390
The next shelter. 
This way!

171
00:19:41,470 --> 00:19:43,470
Yeah!

172
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,930
<i>Whoo-hoo!</i>

173
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:10,210
I'll see if it's safe.

174
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:18,930
- Stay back! 
- Come, Ziza.

175
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:39,070
Come!

176
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:37,590
Lajjun and Ziza!

177
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:40,340
- When it's over. 
- Let me go. I must get to my family!

178
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:42,760
When it's over.

179
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:12,710
Aah!

180
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:44,240
In here.

181
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:47,740
Get in.

182
00:22:49,450 --> 00:22:51,660
Shh.

183
00:23:55,850 --> 00:23:58,440
<i>- Imam! 
- Don't follow me.</i>

184
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:35,990
There will be 
an afterlife for me.

185
00:25:37,660 --> 00:25:39,580
Will there be for you?

186
00:26:57,530 --> 00:27:01,080
Let's go replenish the ranks.

187
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:38,610
In this 'verse,

188
00:27:38,700 --> 00:27:42,790
life is antagonistic 
to the natural state.

189
00:27:44,330 --> 00:27:49,380
<i>Here, humans in all 
their various races...</i>

190
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:52,590
are a spontaneous outbreak...

191
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:54,840
an unguided mistake.

192
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:56,920
Our purpose...

193
00:27:57,010 --> 00:28:00,800
is to correct that mistake.

194
00:28:02,010 --> 00:28:05,310
Because there is another 'verse...

195
00:28:05,390 --> 00:28:10,400
a 'verse where life 
is welcomed and cherished.

196
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:16,280
<i>A ravishing, ever-new place 
called UnderVerse.</i>

197
00:28:17,530 --> 00:28:23,120
<i>So it is this 'verse 
that must be cleansed of life,</i>

198
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:27,450
so that UnderVerse 
can populate and prosper.

199
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:34,630
<i>Look around you. 
Every Necromonger in this hall,</i>

200
00:28:34,670 --> 00:28:39,130
every one of the Legion Vast that just 
swept aside your defenses in one night...

201
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:41,970
was once like you.

202
00:28:42,010 --> 00:28:44,760
Fought as feebly as you.

203
00:28:45,850 --> 00:28:48,770
Every Necromonger 
that lives today...

204
00:28:48,850 --> 00:28:50,980
is a convert.

205
00:28:51,020 --> 00:28:56,230
- There'll be no conversions! 
- We all began as something else!

206
00:28:58,530 --> 00:29:02,950
It was hard for me to accept, too, 
when I first heard these words.

207
00:29:03,030 --> 00:29:05,620
But I changed.

208
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:07,120
I let them take away my pain.

209
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:12,290
- You betrayed your faith! 
- Just as you will change...

210
00:29:12,370 --> 00:29:17,800
<i>when you realize that the threshold 
to the UnderVerse will be crossed...</i>

211
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:22,050
<i>only by those who have 
embraced the Necromonger faith.</i>

212
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:25,260
For those of you 
who will right now...

213
00:29:25,350 --> 00:29:29,390
drop to your knees 
and ask to be purified.

214
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:33,020
- We will not renounce our faith! 
- No one here will do what you ask.

215
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,900
It is unthinkable!

216
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:41,320
<i>This is a world of many peoples, 
many religions!</i>

217
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:45,780
And we simply cannot 
and will not be converted!

218
00:29:45,870 --> 00:29:48,660
Then I'll take your soul.

219
00:30:00,010 --> 00:30:02,550
<i>Join him...</i>

220
00:30:02,630 --> 00:30:05,840
Or join me.

221
00:30:25,780 --> 00:30:28,410
This is your one chance.

222
00:30:28,490 --> 00:30:30,950
Take the Lord Marshal's offer 
and bow.

223
00:30:31,040 --> 00:30:33,870
I bow to no man.

224
00:30:41,050 --> 00:30:43,090
He's not a man.

225
00:30:43,130 --> 00:30:46,800
He's the holy Half-Dead 
who has seen the UnderVerse.

226
00:30:46,890 --> 00:30:49,390
Look, I'm not 
with everyone here.

227
00:30:49,470 --> 00:30:52,060
But I will take a piece of him.

228
00:30:58,650 --> 00:31:00,610
A piece you will have.

229
00:31:28,640 --> 00:31:30,640
<i>Stop him!</i>

230
00:31:43,070 --> 00:31:45,490
Irgun. One of my best.

231
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:48,030
If you say so.

232
00:31:51,740 --> 00:31:53,990
What do you think of this blade?

233
00:32:03,750 --> 00:32:06,130
I think it's a half-gram heavy 
on the back end.

234
00:32:06,210 --> 00:32:08,180
In our faith,

235
00:32:08,220 --> 00:32:10,390
you keep what you kill.

236
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:19,730
Are you familiar to me?

237
00:32:22,560 --> 00:32:26,070
Have we met 
on some distant field?

238
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,990
You'd think I'd remember.

239
00:32:30,530 --> 00:32:33,780
You'd think I would too.

240
00:32:33,870 --> 00:32:37,410
Take him before the Quasi-Deads.

241
00:33:20,750 --> 00:33:23,080
Beautiful eyes.

242
00:33:23,130 --> 00:33:25,130
Come.

243
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:31,970
The last six Lord Marshals 
have called this home.

244
00:33:32,050 --> 00:33:34,300
Magnificent, isn't it?

245
00:33:34,390 --> 00:33:38,140
- I might have gone a different way. 
- True of us all.

246
00:33:40,140 --> 00:33:44,270
<i>Converts receiving the mark 
of the Necromonger.</i>

247
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:49,780
They learn how one pain 
can lessen another.

248
00:34:03,870 --> 00:34:05,880
There now.

249
00:34:07,540 --> 00:34:10,840
That is just... perfect.

250
00:34:14,220 --> 00:34:17,430
The more you resist them,

251
00:34:17,510 --> 00:34:19,850
the greater the damage will be.

252
00:34:22,430 --> 00:34:25,480
<i>A new one.</i>

253
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:28,320
<i>You've brought us a new one.</i>

254
00:34:41,870 --> 00:34:44,620
Interesting breeder.

255
00:35:00,680 --> 00:35:03,310
<i>Making entry.</i>

256
00:35:05,940 --> 00:35:08,810
<i>We've entered his neocortex.</i>

257
00:35:08,900 --> 00:35:12,730
<i>- Ahh! The Riddick! 
- Regress.</i>

258
00:35:12,820 --> 00:35:16,450
<i>Scanning fresh memories.</i>

259
00:35:16,530 --> 00:35:19,570
<i>Thoughts of someone called Jack.</i>

260
00:35:19,620 --> 00:35:21,540
Riddick!

261
00:35:23,540 --> 00:35:26,370
<i>Now we find thoughts of an Elemental.</i>

262
00:35:26,460 --> 00:35:29,630
<i>The one race that would slow 
the spread of Necromongers.</i>

263
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:31,960
<i>- Furyans. 
- Furyans.</i>

264
00:35:37,300 --> 00:35:39,470
Where does he come from?

265
00:35:39,550 --> 00:35:44,020
Who are his people? 
These are the things I need to know.

266
00:35:46,020 --> 00:35:48,900
<i>We find energy.</i>

267
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:55,190
<i>We find Furyan energy.</i>

268
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,570
<i>-He's Furyan!</i>

269
00:35:57,990 --> 00:36:00,070
<i>Furyan!</i>

270
00:36:01,780 --> 00:36:04,410
<i>A Furyan survivor!</i>

271
00:36:04,950 --> 00:36:07,750
<i>Kill the Furyan! Kill the Riddick!</i>

272
00:36:07,830 --> 00:36:10,790
<i>Kill the Riddick! Kill the Riddick! 
Kill the Riddick!</i>

273
00:36:12,250 --> 00:36:13,340
Kill the Riddick.

274
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:50,210
Find him. Whatever it takes. Find him!

275
00:37:24,990 --> 00:37:29,080
Let me guess. 
A five-man crew this time.

276
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:32,370
Couple of things 
you could have done better.

277
00:37:36,710 --> 00:37:41,340
First, trash the locator beacon 
inside my ship... the one you jacked.

278
00:37:41,420 --> 00:37:44,760
<i>And second... and this is really 
the more important part...</i>

279
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:48,060
dust my dick 
when you get the chance.

280
00:37:48,140 --> 00:37:51,890
- Any questions? 
- Yeah.

281
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:56,060
What took you so long?

282
00:38:21,010 --> 00:38:23,010
<i>Decoy launched.</i>

283
00:38:23,260 --> 00:38:27,390
In and out, unsuspected and undetected. 
Damn, I love a good smash-and-grab.

284
00:38:27,470 --> 00:38:27,680
Not so fast. Not so fast.

285
00:38:28,930 --> 00:38:31,890
<i>- Preparing to engage ion drive. 
- So,</i>

286
00:38:31,930 --> 00:38:35,850
where do we drop 
your merc-killin' ass?

287
00:38:35,940 --> 00:38:38,230
<i>Who's gonna pay 
the most for you now?</i>

288
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:42,070
- Butcher Bay? 
- Butcher Bay.

289
00:38:42,110 --> 00:38:44,900
Ten minutes every other day 
on the dog run.

290
00:38:44,950 --> 00:38:47,950
Protein waffles aren't bad.

291
00:38:47,990 --> 00:38:51,870
Hey, how 'bout Ursa Luna? 
Nice little double-max prison.

292
00:38:51,950 --> 00:38:56,330
They keep a cell open for me... 
just in case I drop in.

293
00:38:56,420 --> 00:38:58,340
<i>You know the problem 
with these joints now?</i>

294
00:38:58,420 --> 00:39:01,380
Health clubs 
for waffle-eatin' pussies.

295
00:39:01,460 --> 00:39:04,170
Maybe we should think about 
uppin' our game here a little bit.

296
00:39:04,260 --> 00:39:06,630
Think about someplace 
truly diabolical.

297
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:08,680
What the hell is he thinkin' now?

298
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:11,260
<i>He's thinkin' a triple-max prison.</i>

299
00:39:11,350 --> 00:39:14,730
<i>A no-daylight slam. 
Only three of 'em left in this system...</i>

300
00:39:14,810 --> 00:39:19,110
two of 'em outta range for a shitty little 
under cutter like this one with no legs.

301
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:22,730
Leavin' just... one...

302
00:39:22,820 --> 00:39:25,740
Crematoria.

303
00:39:25,780 --> 00:39:28,620
That is what you had in mind, 
right, Toombs?

304
00:39:28,660 --> 00:39:31,160
Hey, how does he know where we're goin', 
and we don't?

305
00:39:31,620 --> 00:39:32,330
Dope it out.

306
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:33,500
I hate this run.

307
00:39:33,790 --> 00:39:35,460
Just do it!

308
00:39:35,870 --> 00:39:37,870
Don't know about this 
new crew of yours.

309
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:40,090
They seem a bit skittish.

310
00:39:40,380 --> 00:39:44,880
Probably shouldn't tell 'em 
what happened to the last crew.

311
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:57,100
You know, you supposed 
to be some slick-shit killer.

312
00:39:57,190 --> 00:39:59,690
Now look at you...

313
00:39:59,770 --> 00:40:02,940
all back-of-the-bus 
and shit.

314
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:42,190
<i>I say we attack Helion Two next.</i>

315
00:40:42,230 --> 00:40:44,190
Take it straight 
into their teeth.

316
00:40:44,230 --> 00:40:47,650
It'll cost you 20,000 heads, five 
warrior ships. Nothing more, I swear it.

317
00:40:47,740 --> 00:40:51,030
While I do prize brute force,

318
00:40:51,110 --> 00:40:54,240
this approach 
is perhaps more artful.

319
00:40:54,330 --> 00:40:57,160
Start at the end.

320
00:40:57,250 --> 00:40:59,210
Go straight to Helion Five,

321
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:01,500
the last planet 
in the system.

322
00:41:01,580 --> 00:41:04,210
We approach from the night side.

323
00:41:04,250 --> 00:41:07,260
<i>Remove these cannon first,</i>

324
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:10,130
then attack 
the larger placements at speed.

325
00:41:10,220 --> 00:41:13,010
<i>We'll catch them on their rear flank. 
And in ten days' time,</i>

326
00:41:13,090 --> 00:41:17,390
<i>the rest of those worlds 
will tumble before us.</i>

327
00:41:17,470 --> 00:41:19,810
You see, as with most, 
their blind spot...

328
00:41:19,890 --> 00:41:22,190
is right behind them.

329
00:41:24,270 --> 00:41:27,820
I've located an ion trail 
which leads off-world.

330
00:41:27,900 --> 00:41:30,570
Then you should be 
off-world, Vaako.

331
00:41:30,650 --> 00:41:33,240
I've deployed a tracker team. 
One of the best.

332
00:41:33,320 --> 00:41:37,080
Wherever Riddick has gone, 
you lens him out and cleanse him.

333
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:38,790
You.

334
00:41:38,790 --> 00:41:41,960
You want me to take a 
frigate for one breeder?

335
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:44,170
Don't question it, Vaako!

336
00:41:46,090 --> 00:41:49,260
Take it on faith.

337
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:57,220
<i>Mercenaries, Elementals, 
Necromongers...</i>

338
00:41:57,350 --> 00:42:00,060
<i>Shit, I've never been so popular.</i>

339
00:42:01,350 --> 00:42:05,560
<i>Should probably slip these chains 
and open up a few arteries.</i>

340
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:09,480
<i>But why drive, 
when you can get driven?</i>

341
00:42:09,610 --> 00:42:13,400
<i>A free ticket to Crematoria. 
Thanks, Toombs.</i>

342
00:42:14,280 --> 00:42:17,370
<i>Got me some business there 
named Jack.</i>

343
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:23,040
<i>And once we settle up, 
I'll walk away forever.</i>

344
00:42:23,160 --> 00:42:26,790
<i>So, I'll just wait, all back-of-the-bus.</i>

345
00:42:27,710 --> 00:42:29,380
<i>For now.</i>

346
00:42:43,770 --> 00:42:47,610
- How unexpected. 
- An Elemental.

347
00:42:47,650 --> 00:42:51,280
<i>- Here? 
- One of the captives.</i>

348
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:54,280
<i>And why, after 30 years,</i>

349
00:42:54,320 --> 00:42:56,570
should it be you?

350
00:42:56,780 --> 00:42:59,530
You be the good warrior.

351
00:42:59,620 --> 00:43:02,500
Go after this Riddick.

352
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:06,210
I'll find out why the Lord Marshal 
is so threatened by him.

353
00:43:17,970 --> 00:43:20,390
<i>Destination reached.</i>

354
00:43:20,470 --> 00:43:22,390
<i>Unlocking manual controls.</i>

355
00:43:22,470 --> 00:43:25,810
All right. I make 700 degrees 
on the day side,

356
00:43:24,980 --> 00:43:27,850
300 below on the night side.

357
00:43:27,940 --> 00:43:30,900
Let's not get caught in the sun.

358
00:43:30,980 --> 00:43:33,400
If I owned this place and hell,

359
00:43:33,480 --> 00:43:36,450
I'd rent this place out 
and live in hell.

360
00:43:45,200 --> 00:43:47,620
<i>- Blue angle... good. 
- Stand by.</i>

361
00:43:49,130 --> 00:43:51,090
<i>And...</i>

362
00:43:51,170 --> 00:43:53,130
<i>Plotted course good.</i>

363
00:43:53,170 --> 00:43:55,590
Hit it!

364
00:43:55,670 --> 00:43:59,470
<i>Angle of approach, not good.</i>

365
00:44:06,850 --> 00:44:09,520
<i>Look, Ma. No hands!</i>

366
00:44:43,970 --> 00:44:45,890
Party poppers!

367
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:10,710
I think I shit myself.

368
00:45:11,920 --> 00:45:15,090
Skittish, Toombs. Very skittish.

369
00:45:36,610 --> 00:45:38,570
Comfy?

370
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:59,380
When the ride's over,

371
00:45:59,460 --> 00:46:02,010
your goggles are mine.

372
00:46:30,580 --> 00:46:33,620
Four-way split!

373
00:46:43,970 --> 00:46:46,260
29.4 kilometers.

374
00:46:54,770 --> 00:46:59,110
So, this is Riddick.

375
00:47:23,760 --> 00:47:27,800
What in the bowels of Christ 
are you talkin' about, 700K?

376
00:47:27,890 --> 00:47:29,760
Don't take this one, boss.

377
00:47:29,850 --> 00:47:33,140
See? Anatoli here 
has a nose for trouble.

378
00:47:33,220 --> 00:47:35,560
And this one, this Riddick guy...

379
00:47:35,640 --> 00:47:37,730
Big, big trouble.

380
00:47:37,810 --> 00:47:40,940
So, 700,000 is good money.

381
00:47:41,020 --> 00:47:44,780
I'd take the money, Toombs.

382
00:47:52,490 --> 00:47:57,040
<i>The guild pays us a caretaker's fee 
for each prisoner each year.</i>

383
00:47:57,080 --> 00:48:01,130
We pay mercs 20% of that total fee 
based on a certain life expectancy.

384
00:48:01,210 --> 00:48:02,840
<i>How's about this?</i>

385
00:48:02,920 --> 00:48:05,840
You open that safe you got hidden 
behind the console there,

386
00:48:05,920 --> 00:48:10,050
show me the real books, 
then we figure out my cut.

387
00:48:10,090 --> 00:48:12,100
Then I'll be on my way.

388
00:48:16,980 --> 00:48:20,350
Open my books. 
This is what you suggest?

389
00:48:25,400 --> 00:48:27,360
Wasn't a suggestion.

390
00:48:45,250 --> 00:48:49,970
<i>These are dangerous days, 
if you believe the talk.</i>

391
00:48:50,970 --> 00:48:54,010
- Talk? 
- About dead planets.

392
00:48:54,100 --> 00:48:57,220
About some ghost army.

393
00:48:57,310 --> 00:48:59,940
About them.

394
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:03,480
"Them"?

395
00:49:20,250 --> 00:49:22,170
I'll run the numbers again.

396
00:49:22,250 --> 00:49:24,340
It takes a couple of days, 
probably,

397
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:27,800
so you can stay as my guest.

398
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:29,840
At least here, we are all safe.

399
00:49:29,880 --> 00:49:33,180
<i>- Yes? 
- Yes, boss.</i>

400
00:49:33,260 --> 00:49:35,640
I'll give it a day.

401
00:49:38,020 --> 00:49:40,140
One.

402
00:50:18,560 --> 00:50:20,520
<i>There are inmates...</i>

403
00:50:20,560 --> 00:50:23,310
<i>and there are convicts.</i>

404
00:50:23,390 --> 00:50:26,810
A convict has a certain code.

405
00:50:26,900 --> 00:50:30,860
And he knows to show 
a certain respect.

406
00:50:31,900 --> 00:50:34,450
<i>An inmate, on the other hand,</i>

407
00:50:34,530 --> 00:50:37,030
pulls the pin on his fellow man.

408
00:50:37,120 --> 00:50:39,540
<i>Does the guards' work for them.</i>

409
00:50:39,580 --> 00:50:42,200
Brings shame...

410
00:50:42,250 --> 00:50:44,620
To the game.

411
00:50:46,630 --> 00:50:49,590
So, which are you gonna be?

412
00:50:49,670 --> 00:50:52,210
Me?

413
00:50:54,300 --> 00:50:56,590
I'm just passin' through.

414
00:51:02,430 --> 00:51:04,560
Welcome to Crematoria.

415
00:51:25,290 --> 00:51:29,960
They can be quite a test, 
these deep runs...

416
00:51:31,800 --> 00:51:33,960
tests of our inner selves.

417
00:51:36,300 --> 00:51:38,680
Don't you find that true?

418
00:51:42,640 --> 00:51:44,640
Some men do.

419
00:51:46,060 --> 00:51:48,600
<i>Just being so far from the armada,</i>

420
00:51:48,650 --> 00:51:54,530
the mind can start to fill 
with strange thoughts, doubts.

421
00:51:54,610 --> 00:51:57,530
Don't you ever have doubts, Vaako?

422
00:52:00,990 --> 00:52:03,450
- Doubts? 
- About the campaign.

423
00:52:04,500 --> 00:52:06,620
About Lord Marshal.

424
00:52:08,670 --> 00:52:13,000
First and always, 
I am a Necromonger commander.

425
00:52:14,090 --> 00:52:19,180
So if you're here to test my loyalty, 
you succeed only in testing my patience.

426
00:52:19,260 --> 00:52:22,850
Oh, no. 
No, that's not why I'm here at all.

427
00:52:29,060 --> 00:52:32,440
<i>A young warrior 
once consulted a seer.</i>

428
00:52:33,440 --> 00:52:38,490
<i>He was told a child would be born 
on the planet Furya... a male child...</i>

429
00:52:38,570 --> 00:52:41,780
<i>who would someday 
cause the warrior's downfall.</i>

430
00:52:41,780 --> 00:52:45,160
<i>Cause his untimed death.</i>

431
00:52:46,160 --> 00:52:51,130
Furya? Furya's a ruined world. 
No life to speak of.

432
00:52:51,210 --> 00:52:52,750
For good reason.

433
00:52:52,840 --> 00:52:57,840
This young warrior 
mounted an attack on Furya,

434
00:52:57,880 --> 00:53:01,010
killing all young males 
he could find,

435
00:53:01,050 --> 00:53:05,180
even strangling some 
with their birth cords.

436
00:53:05,220 --> 00:53:08,020
An artful stroke, 
wouldn't you say?

437
00:53:09,940 --> 00:53:13,980
So this warrior, the one who tried to 
outwit the prediction, would later become...

438
00:53:14,060 --> 00:53:16,070
That's why he worries.

439
00:53:16,150 --> 00:53:18,150
...our Lord Marshal.

440
00:53:19,740 --> 00:53:21,740
Which would make 
the man-child...

441
00:53:21,820 --> 00:53:24,280
He worries he missed 
killing that child in its crib.

442
00:53:24,370 --> 00:53:26,370
...Riddick.

443
00:54:20,260 --> 00:54:22,680
Feeding time!

444
00:54:29,930 --> 00:54:32,560
Here they come!

445
00:55:35,080 --> 00:55:38,420
Aaah!

446
00:57:03,500 --> 00:57:05,500
It's an animal thing.

447
00:57:12,300 --> 00:57:15,430
Let's pop the cork. 
Get some fresh air.

448
00:57:52,550 --> 00:57:54,640
So they do go topside...

449
00:57:56,050 --> 00:57:58,810
to swap out air.

450
00:57:58,890 --> 00:58:01,310
Interesting.

451
00:58:01,390 --> 00:58:03,100
Who the hell are you?

452
00:58:05,060 --> 00:58:08,440
When it happens, it'll happen fast.

453
00:58:08,530 --> 00:58:11,990
<i>Stay on my leg when I cut fence 
or stay here...</i>

454
00:58:12,030 --> 00:58:14,030
for the rest of your unnatural life.

455
00:58:14,110 --> 00:58:17,950
Nobody outs this place. 
Nobody.

456
00:58:24,000 --> 00:58:26,340
<i>He ain't "nobody. "</i>

457
00:58:40,390 --> 00:58:44,770
<i>Good news first. 
Talked things over with my amigos here.</i>

458
00:58:44,850 --> 00:58:48,070
We'll cut you in for 775K.

459
00:58:50,530 --> 00:58:52,570
Well, all right.

460
00:58:52,650 --> 00:58:54,990
What's the bad news? 
They close the local whorehouse?

461
00:58:57,700 --> 00:59:01,450
<i>No. The bad news is worse than that. 
Much worse.</i>

462
00:59:01,540 --> 00:59:06,540
Our pilot, he saw this. 
It crossed a shipping lane.

463
00:59:10,090 --> 00:59:13,590
<i>Any idea what this might be?</i>

464
00:59:17,220 --> 00:59:20,180
Never saw nothin' like it.

465
00:59:20,260 --> 00:59:23,980
<i>This ship charts back 
to Helion Prime.</i>

466
00:59:24,060 --> 00:59:27,560
You know, Anatoli's 
got a nose for trouble,

467
00:59:27,650 --> 00:59:30,770
<i>and he thinks 
trouble follows you here.</i>

468
00:59:33,820 --> 00:59:38,160
<i>Look. We dusted our tracks 
and got the hell outta there.</i>

469
00:59:38,200 --> 00:59:41,200
There is no way 
we didn't lose them.

470
00:59:42,370 --> 00:59:45,250
"Them"?

471
00:59:50,710 --> 00:59:53,920
This is my prisoner. Mine.

472
00:59:54,010 --> 00:59:56,010
Nobody else's.

473
00:59:56,090 --> 00:59:58,390
And I want my money now.

474
00:59:58,470 --> 01:00:00,550
<i>So...</i>

475
01:00:00,640 --> 01:00:03,060
you stole a prisoner...

476
01:00:03,140 --> 01:00:05,140
from "them"?

477
01:01:12,380 --> 01:01:14,590
No.

478
01:01:14,670 --> 01:01:17,760
<i>Riddick. No!</i>

479
01:01:22,970 --> 01:01:26,930
Shoulda taken the money, Toombs.

480
01:02:22,900 --> 01:02:25,450
You gonna kill me?

481
01:02:58,770 --> 01:03:00,980
<i>Mercs.</i>

482
01:03:02,440 --> 01:03:04,910
Some guards here, 
but this can't be all of them.

483
01:03:06,110 --> 01:03:09,410
<i>Check their slots in the back... 
and be careful.</i>

484
01:03:09,490 --> 01:03:10,580
<i>Don't bother.</i>

485
01:03:11,580 --> 01:03:13,960
Guards ain't there.

486
01:03:14,040 --> 01:03:16,750
<i>They figured out the Necros 
are comin' for me.</i>

487
01:03:16,830 --> 01:03:20,000
Plan was to clean the bank, 
ghost the mercs,

488
01:03:20,090 --> 01:03:22,010
break wide through the tunnel.

489
01:03:22,090 --> 01:03:25,800
And then somebody got a lucky shot off 
with this rocket launcher here...

490
01:03:25,880 --> 01:03:27,890
and took out the sled.

491
01:03:27,970 --> 01:03:32,100
Guards took off on foot but rigged 
the door so no one could follow.

492
01:03:33,140 --> 01:03:37,730
<i>They'll take the one ship in the hangar 
and leave everyone else here to die.</i>

493
01:03:37,810 --> 01:03:41,190
How come you know all this shit?

494
01:03:41,270 --> 01:03:43,280
You weren't even here.

495
01:03:44,320 --> 01:03:46,400
'Cause it was my plan.

496
01:03:52,160 --> 01:03:54,700
I shoulda taken the money.

497
01:04:00,590 --> 01:04:03,670
Riddick!

498
01:04:14,270 --> 01:04:17,390
<i>What is this? 
What is he thinking?</i>

499
01:04:17,480 --> 01:04:20,440
<i>- Once that sun comes up... 
- We'll last five minutes.</i>

500
01:04:20,480 --> 01:04:24,440
Five minutes. We ain't gonna last 
30 seconds out there.

501
01:04:24,530 --> 01:04:26,530
It'll light you up like a match.

502
01:04:31,120 --> 01:04:35,290
20-mile buffer zone 
and 30 klicks to the hangar.

503
01:04:37,460 --> 01:04:40,710
30 klicks over that terrain?

504
01:04:52,350 --> 01:04:57,390
It's moving in the right direction. 
We could make it.

505
01:04:57,770 --> 01:05:00,480
Stay behind the night,

506
01:05:00,520 --> 01:05:02,860
ahead of the sun.

507
01:05:02,900 --> 01:05:05,230
There's gonna be one speed...

508
01:05:07,360 --> 01:05:09,320
mine.

509
01:05:11,620 --> 01:05:13,780
<i>If you can't keep up, don't step up.</i>

510
01:05:13,870 --> 01:05:15,790
You'll just die.

511
01:06:19,930 --> 01:06:21,690
<i>Riddick?</i>

512
01:06:23,770 --> 01:06:25,730
Riddick?

513
01:06:29,110 --> 01:06:31,110
Riddick?

514
01:06:35,620 --> 01:06:39,160
Go, go! Go on! Go! Climb here!

515
01:06:39,240 --> 01:06:41,910
Climb! Go! Go, go, go!

516
01:07:07,610 --> 01:07:09,440
Boss!

517
01:07:13,280 --> 01:07:15,240
<i>Up there.</i>

518
01:07:15,320 --> 01:07:17,490
- Take a look. 
- Because Anatoli says so?

519
01:07:17,570 --> 01:07:20,660
Because his nose says so.

520
01:07:37,970 --> 01:07:40,510
There's nothin' up here.

521
01:07:42,600 --> 01:07:44,020
Oh, shit.

522
01:07:53,820 --> 01:07:56,360
Riddick.

523
01:07:56,450 --> 01:08:00,070
<i>They're heading right for the volcano 
fields. They're going for our ship!</i>

524
01:08:00,160 --> 01:08:02,740
No chance do they get to 
the hangar first. No chance!

525
01:08:14,550 --> 01:08:16,720
Next one! Next hole! 
We'll catch 'em there!

526
01:08:44,660 --> 01:08:46,960
<i>No more run for you.</i>

527
01:08:52,170 --> 01:08:55,590
Where did the big guy go?

528
01:09:01,340 --> 01:09:03,300
Ohh...

529
01:09:28,370 --> 01:09:30,120
Close it!

530
01:10:01,700 --> 01:10:04,530
What was that? 
You don't care if you live or die?

531
01:10:04,620 --> 01:10:07,620
If I kill them first, not really.

532
01:10:09,290 --> 01:10:11,370
Maybe I do.

533
01:10:11,460 --> 01:10:13,460
Keep moving!

534
01:11:10,770 --> 01:11:13,850
<i>Kyra?</i>

535
01:11:13,940 --> 01:11:16,600
Get that ass moving!

536
01:11:57,480 --> 01:11:58,980
"One speed. "

537
01:12:19,580 --> 01:12:21,460
Temperature differential.

538
01:12:21,540 --> 01:12:24,010
Your rope.

539
01:12:23,170 --> 01:12:26,470
It's too late. 
We're never gonna make it.

540
01:12:26,550 --> 01:12:28,630
Your rope! Gimme your rope!

541
01:12:29,760 --> 01:12:31,850
And your water. All of it!

542
01:12:32,890 --> 01:12:36,350
Stay in the shadow of the mountain. 
Don't wait for me. Run!

543
01:12:48,240 --> 01:12:50,620
Riddick!

544
01:13:01,670 --> 01:13:03,090
Aaah!

545
01:13:34,580 --> 01:13:36,490
Where the hell is that hangar?

546
01:13:41,500 --> 01:13:45,290
<i>There it is.</i>

547
01:13:47,300 --> 01:13:51,590
<i>Listen.</i>

548
01:14:16,910 --> 01:14:16,950
Let me guess. Necros.

549
01:14:44,900 --> 01:14:50,030
I figure we got three minutes before the sun 
hits us again, burns out this whole valley.

550
01:14:50,110 --> 01:14:52,820
- Wait. 
- We gonna do this or not?

551
01:14:52,900 --> 01:14:54,780
Just wait.

552
01:15:12,050 --> 01:15:14,630
Aaah! Boss!

553
01:15:46,750 --> 01:15:48,460
On the right!

554
01:15:55,970 --> 01:15:57,760
Watch out! 
Behind you!

555
01:15:57,840 --> 01:15:59,600
<i>Kyra!</i>

556
01:16:55,650 --> 01:16:57,700
Sybar!

557
01:17:59,220 --> 01:18:01,180
<i>No!</i>

558
01:19:47,700 --> 01:19:49,910
Kyra?

559
01:19:53,790 --> 01:19:56,710
<i>I was supposed to 
deliver a message to you...</i>

560
01:19:58,710 --> 01:20:01,000
if Vaako failed to kill you.

561
01:20:02,880 --> 01:20:05,670
A message from 
the Lord Marshal himself.

562
01:20:07,550 --> 01:20:11,060
He tells you to stay away from Helion, 
stay away from him,

563
01:20:12,390 --> 01:20:14,520
and in return, 
you'll be hunted no more.

564
01:20:21,520 --> 01:20:24,360
But Vaako will most likely 
report you as dead.

565
01:20:25,740 --> 01:20:28,030
So this is your chance.

566
01:20:27,150 --> 01:20:31,870
Your chance to do 
what no man has ever done.

567
01:20:31,910 --> 01:20:33,910
The girl.

568
01:20:34,950 --> 01:20:36,330
Where will they take her?

569
01:20:37,870 --> 01:20:41,380
We all began... as something else.

570
01:20:44,630 --> 01:20:47,340
I've done... unbelievable things...

571
01:20:44,760 --> 01:20:46,470
I've done... unbelievable things...

572
01:20:48,340 --> 01:20:50,220
in the name of a faith 
that was never my own.

573
01:20:53,010 --> 01:20:56,980
And he'll do to her 
what he did to me.

574
01:21:03,230 --> 01:21:07,860
The Necromonger in me 
warns you not to go back.

575
01:21:09,200 --> 01:21:11,820
But the Furyan in me...

576
01:21:15,370 --> 01:21:17,120
hopes you won't listen.

577
01:22:24,190 --> 01:22:27,070
<i>I have lost a Purifier...</i>

578
01:22:28,320 --> 01:22:33,110
<i>but I have gained 
a first among commanders.</i>

579
01:22:34,110 --> 01:22:36,740
It is overdue, isn't it...

580
01:22:36,830 --> 01:22:39,500
that we acknowledge 
your many accomplishments,

581
01:22:39,580 --> 01:22:40,830
<i>your steady faith,</i>

582
01:22:41,830 --> 01:22:47,340
and above all, 
your unflinching loyalty.

583
01:22:55,090 --> 01:22:58,600
Obedience without question. 
Loyalty till UnderVerse come.

584
01:23:01,100 --> 01:23:03,100
Well done, Vaako.

585
01:23:04,350 --> 01:23:07,980
This is a day of days.

586
01:23:28,130 --> 01:23:30,670
<i>Now, tell me if it's true.</i>

587
01:23:30,710 --> 01:23:34,970
Tell me the Furyan is gone, and I can close 
this campaign without hearing his bootsteps.

588
01:23:35,550 --> 01:23:38,470
If he is dead,

589
01:23:39,640 --> 01:23:41,680
I sense I'm not far 
from the same fate,

590
01:23:42,730 --> 01:23:44,690
being of no further use here.

591
01:23:45,730 --> 01:23:48,810
Shouldn't I tell you 
that Riddick is still alive?

592
01:23:48,900 --> 01:23:50,690
Don't try me, Aereon.

593
01:23:50,730 --> 01:23:53,030
I could plough you under 
with the rest of Helion Prime.

594
01:23:53,070 --> 01:23:55,400
No one really knows the future.

595
01:23:55,490 --> 01:23:59,280
Then tell me the odds 
that Vaako met with success,

596
01:23:59,370 --> 01:24:01,370
that I will now be the one...

597
01:24:01,410 --> 01:24:04,330
who can carry his people across 
the threshold into UnderVerse,

598
01:24:04,410 --> 01:24:06,370
where they shall begin true life.

599
01:24:06,460 --> 01:24:08,750
Tell me what I want to hear, Aereon,

600
01:24:08,830 --> 01:24:12,920
and maybe 
I'll save your home world... for last.

601
01:24:17,760 --> 01:24:19,340
- The odds are good...

602
01:24:21,810 --> 01:24:24,060
That Riddick is still alive

603
01:25:02,430 --> 01:25:04,260
Ascension protocol!

604
01:25:04,310 --> 01:25:08,020
We still have numbers out there, Lord 
Marshal... sweep teams, recon ships.

605
01:25:08,100 --> 01:25:10,150
They would be hard-pressed 
to make it back...

606
01:25:14,940 --> 01:25:18,780
Get my armada off the ground!

607
01:26:38,360 --> 01:26:41,900
Final protocol. 
Execute on my order.

608
01:27:16,810 --> 01:27:18,110
Go inside.

609
01:28:10,490 --> 01:28:12,740
<i>We found this Lensor dead.</i>

610
01:28:15,330 --> 01:28:18,750
<i>Show me his last sight.</i>

611
01:28:31,180 --> 01:28:32,850
Commander Toal.

612
01:28:32,930 --> 01:28:34,930
He won't escape twice.

613
01:30:27,300 --> 01:30:30,420
Stay your weapons!

614
01:30:31,880 --> 01:30:33,890
He came for me.

615
01:31:00,660 --> 01:31:02,080
<i>Consider this:</i>

616
01:31:07,880 --> 01:31:11,970
<i>If you fall here now,</i>

617
01:31:12,050 --> 01:31:14,010
you'll never rise.

618
01:31:14,050 --> 01:31:17,180
<i>But if you choose another way...</i>

619
01:31:18,350 --> 01:31:20,520
<i>the Necromonger way...</i>

620
01:31:20,600 --> 01:31:23,140
<i>you'll die in due time...</i>

621
01:31:23,190 --> 01:31:26,940
and rise again in the UnderVerse.

622
01:31:36,570 --> 01:31:38,780
Go to him.

623
01:31:46,290 --> 01:31:48,290
It hurts...

624
01:31:49,290 --> 01:31:51,550
at first.

625
01:31:51,630 --> 01:31:55,220
But after a while, the pain 
goes away, just as they promise.

626
01:31:57,640 --> 01:32:00,180
- Are you with me, Kyra? 
- There's a moment...

627
01:32:00,220 --> 01:32:02,640
when you can almost 
see the UnderVerse through his eyes.

628
01:32:03,980 --> 01:32:06,730
It makes it sound perfect...

629
01:32:06,810 --> 01:32:08,730
a place where anyone 
can start over.

630
01:32:08,810 --> 01:32:11,270
Are you with me, Kyra?

631
01:32:23,830 --> 01:32:26,250
Convert now...

632
01:32:26,330 --> 01:32:28,500
or fall forever.

633
01:32:33,260 --> 01:32:35,550
You killed everything I know.

634
01:32:40,680 --> 01:32:41,890
Vaako.

635
01:32:43,970 --> 01:32:46,230
Not yet.

636
01:32:57,780 --> 01:33:00,780
Been a long time 
since I've seen my own blood.

637
01:34:19,030 --> 01:34:22,030
These are his last moments.

638
01:34:41,630 --> 01:34:44,470
Give me your soul.

639
01:34:49,520 --> 01:34:50,230
Never!

640
01:35:58,210 --> 01:36:00,460
You're not the one to bring me down.

641
01:36:37,040 --> 01:36:40,080
Help me, Vaako. Kill him.

642
01:36:47,720 --> 01:36:49,050
Vaako?

643
01:36:53,720 --> 01:36:55,560
Forgive me.

644
01:37:38,850 --> 01:37:41,440
I thought you were dead.

645
01:37:43,690 --> 01:37:46,280
Are you with me, Kyra?

646
01:37:48,320 --> 01:37:50,910
I was always with you.

647
01:37:53,240 --> 01:37:55,240
I was.

648
01:39:18,910 --> 01:39:20,750
You keep what you kill.
